## Story Description
Two deprecation warnings appear across the test run. First, src/ingestion/cleaner.py has two calls to df.select_dtypes(include=['object']) (at approximately lines 176 and 182) that trigger Pandas4Warning. The forward-compatible fix is select_dtypes(include=['object', 'string']). Second, src/ingestion/ingest.py calls datetime.utcnow() (approximately line 144) which is deprecated since Python 3.12. Fix by importing timezone from datetime and changing to datetime.now(timezone.utc).

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/ingestion/cleaner.py — change both occurrences of select_dtypes(include=['object']) to select_dtypes(include=['object', 'string'])
- Edit file: src/ingestion/ingest.py — ensure 'timezone' is in the datetime import (e.g. from datetime import datetime, timezone), then change datetime.utcnow() to datetime.now(timezone.utc)
- Run: python3 -m pytest tests/ -v 2>&1 | grep -c 'Pandas4Warning' — output must be 0
- Run: python3 -m pytest tests/ -v 2>&1 | grep 'utcnow' — must return empty (no matches)
- Run: python3 -m pytest tests/ -v 2>&1 | tail -5 — must show 0 failed (no regressions)

